Call Global SimTalk Functions from the Python Code
To call a global SimTalk function from the Python code, you first have to import the PlantSimulation
module.
For this module you can then call the predefined functions which Plant Simulation provides.
Call Global SimTalk Functions from the Python Code
11-3740 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
import PlantSimulation as ps
x = ps.existsObject(".Models.Model.EventController")
print(x)
The result looks like this when we Import the PythonModule.
See also
Predefined Functions
Call Global SimTalk Functions from the Python Code
Plant Simulation Help 11-3741
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Call a Function Written in a Another PythonModule
To call and execute a function written in one PythonModule from a different PythonModule, you need to
get the name of the PythonModule you want to import.
In our example we want to import python code we wrote in PythonModule1 into our PythonModule.
To do so, call the function print(__name__) in PythonModule1. This prints the name of the module to the
Console.
Then copy the string from the Console and paste in after the keyword import into the PythonModule
where you want to execute it.
Call a Function Written in a Another PythonModule
11-3742 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Click Import. This prints the result of the multiplication to the Plant Simulation Console.
