Execute External Python Code
To execute Python code, which you wrote and stored in an external file, use the SimTalk function
executePythonFile.
Example
print executePythonFile("D:\test.py", "TestArg")
You can access the objects in your Plant Simulation model in the same way as you would when executing
the Python code using a PythonModule.
